		<help>
			<title>MD-500E</title>
			<key>
				<name>{ }</name>
				<desc>Auto shutdown/start turbines</desc>
			</key>
			<line> NOTE. using autostart will not trigger all functions the way the manual start does.</line>

			<key>
				<name>r</name>
				<desc>apply rotor brake</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>R</name>
				<desc>toggle rotor brake</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>MMB</name>
				<desc>adjust power level (middle mouse button + scroll mouse up/down )</desc>
			</key>
			<line>MTOW 3000lb Gross. MTOW for External loads 3550lb Gross.</line>
			<line></line>
			<line>All lights are default to the OFF position. Light switches can be found on the main panel </line>
			<line>Radio equipment only functions when the power is on  via the batter or generator switches </line>
			<line></line>
			<line>Emergancy Floatation system:-</line>
			<line>The floats are available  through the EQUIPMENT-FUEL + PAYLOAD menu.</line>
			<line>Once fitted the arming and trigger systems become available in the cockpit.</line>
			<line>On the Main panel, a red Arming switch will be available, which lights up red when the system is armed</line>
			<line>On the left side of the main panel, the red Trigger toggle will become available.</line>
			<line>Once the system is armed, clicking the trigger will infate the floats.</line>
			<line> Clicking the trigger again while on dry land will repack the floats and re set the system</line>
			<line></line>
			<line>Manual start:-</line>
			<line>Battery switch  to ON ( main panel )</line>
			<line>PITOT Heat - ON ( Main Panel )</line>
			<line>Engine heat as required ( main panel )</line>
			<line>Nav and beacons -ON ( main panel )</line>
			<line>Landing light - as required  ( main panel )</line>
			<line>Instrument lighting - as required ( main panel )</line>
			<line>Fuel pump - ON ( main panel )</line>
			<line>Set engine to Idle position -  63% (  Press Middle mouse button and scroll mouse up )</line>
			<line>Press the starter button ( red button, right side of the collective )</line>
			<line>On main RPM Gauge, wait until the engine needle is at 20%, then disengage the starter  ( click the red button again)</line>
			<line>Engine and Rotor RPM should now climb to  idle position</line>
			<line>Once at Idle,  Turn on the Generator, then turn off the Battery  ( switches are side by side on the main paael )</line>
			<line>Fuel pump to  OFF </line>
			<line>Increase  engine power to 97% and then you are ready to fly </line>
			<line></line>
			<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your chopper, you can use this menu option to call on another 500E</line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>
<line></line>
<line>If you are using HDR, then you need to enable the specific HDR panel lights from the MD-500E Menu.</line>
 <line>Using the HDR panel lights while not in HDR will produce very strange results.</line>
			<line> </line>

		</help>
